{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1522216-ai-chat-as-a-possible-storyteller-s-tool","id":1522216,"title":"AI Chat as a possible Storyteller's Tool","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-07T06:35:54-07:00","id":1522216,"title":"AI Chat as a possible Storyteller's Tool","content":"So while I'm wary of AI writers such as Chat GPT taking the place of actual research and effort I've found a few uses for it, for example the other week my PCs went to the city's Temple of the Sun and spur of the moment I decided that people would be singing when they arrived but didn't have an appropriate song. So I asked Chat GPT for a song about worshiping the Unconquered Sun and got something much better than any of my own songwriting efforts that seem limited to dumb little jingles. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Chat GPT</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Verse 1)<br /> Beneath the heavens' endless arch,<br /> Where legends and destinies spark,<br /> We gather 'neath the blazing light,<br /> Unconquered Sun, our guiding might.<br /> <br /> (Pre-Chorus)<br /> In realms where ancient powers soar,<br /> Your radiance forevermore,<br /> A beacon in the darkest night,<br /> Igniting hope with sacred light.<br /> <br /> (Chorus)<br /> Oh, Unconquered Sun, forever bright,<br /> In your brilliance, we take flight,<br /> With hearts aflame, we raise our voice,<br /> In worship, let our souls rejoice.<br /> <br /> (Verse 2)<br /> Across Creation's vast expanse,<br /> Your presence weaves a sacred dance,<br /> From mountains high to oceans wide,<br /> You bless us with your golden stride.<br /> <br /> (Pre-Chorus)<br /> In battle's heat and honor's quest,<br /> We find in you our strength, our best,<br /> Protector of the weak and just,<br /> In you, our faith and trust we thrust.<br /> <br /> (Chorus)<br /> Oh, Unconquered Sun, forever bright,<br /> In your brilliance, we take flight,<br /> With hearts aflame, we raise our voice,<br /> In worship, let our souls rejoice.<br /> <br /> (Bridge)<br /> A tapestry of stars above,<br /> Reflects your boundless, endless love,<br /> Eternal flame that never wanes,<br /> In your embrace, no darkness reigns.<br /> <br /> (Verse 3)<br /> Through ages past, your stories told,<br /> In songs and sagas, brave and bold,<br /> We honor you with grateful hearts,<br /> As each new day your glory starts.<br /> <br /> (Pre-Chorus)<br /> Guiding essence, celestial fire,<br /> In reverence, our souls aspire,<br /> To emulate your steadfast grace,<br /> And bring your light to every place.<br /> <br /> (Chorus)<br /> Oh, Unconquered Sun, forever bright,<br /> In your brilliance, we take flight,<br /> With hearts aflame, we raise our voice,<br /> In worship, let our souls rejoice.<br /> <br /> (Outro)<br /> As dawn's first rays paint skies anew,<br /> Our gratitude forever true,<br /> Unconquered Sun, forever shine,<br /> In your embrace, our spirits twine.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>AI art, I find is mostly just distracting. I sometimes try and smash together two disassociated ideas to see what the end result might be but I've not as of yet gotten anything that's provided better results than creating a Pinterest board. <br /> <br /> What are other people's opinions on this so far?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T07:47:35-07:00","id":1522218,"title":"","content":"It's good at filler, effectively (which is kind of what you've used it for). The more you use it the more you notice that it trends heavily towards the most prosaic and lukewarm prose, like whatever it is you default to thinking a poem or an essay or the like will end up being. It will seldom write anything you couldn't have written if you had the time to sit down and do it, except when it starts gaslighting you because the output pattern didn't grasp the right parts of your prompt. (I don't want to say &quot;because it didn't understand what you asked for&quot; because, of course, a big part of LLM misuse is users expecting it to &quot;understand&quot; information and output &quot;answers.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T12:36:32-07:00","id":1522228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1522216-ai-chat-as-a-possible-storyteller-s-tool#post1522216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while I'm wary of AI writers such as Chat GPT taking the place of actual research and effort I've found a few uses for it, for example the other week my PCs went to the city's Temple of the Sun and spur of the moment I decided that people would be singing when they arrived but didn't have an appropriate song. So I asked Chat GPT for a song about worshiping the Unconquered Sun and got something much better than any of my own songwriting efforts that seem limited to dumb little jingles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> AI art, I find is mostly just distracting. I sometimes try and smash together two disassociated ideas to see what the end result might be but I've not as of yet gotten anything that's provided better results than creating a Pinterest board.<br /> <br /> What are other people's opinions on this so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>thats awesome, I agree that it probably wouldn't make a good storyteller or GM but I do believe it would be a great asset when you want to offload filler stuff or if you already have a bunch of examples of something and you want the AI to create something else<br /> <br /> as an example I could feed chatgpt all of a splat's official and homebrew charms that are generally considered well balanced and well written and then ask it for new charms or to assist me in creating and balancing new charms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T18:08:30-07:00","id":1522244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1522216-ai-chat-as-a-possible-storyteller-s-tool?p=1522228#post1522228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as an example I could feed chatgpt all of a splat's official and homebrew charms that are generally considered well balanced and well written and then ask it for new charms or to assist me in creating and balancing new charms</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an example of expecting a Large Language Model to &quot;understand&quot; the material it's fed.<br /> <br /> A Large Language Model does one thing: it produces a convincing, plausible, real-<i>sounding</i> answer to a question or prompt. Not an accurate or a well-crafted answer. It's a pattern-matching machine; it finds and matches patterns without understanding the context that produces them. If you feed it Charm text, its output will match the Charm format pattern, having Charm names, costs in motes and Willpower, keywords (but not necessarily always keywords that <i>exist,</i> let alone keywords used correctly for how they work), and descriptions of actions. There is no reason to expect it will be able to associate the relative game balance of different opportunity costs and desired effects.<br /> <br /> You can ask ChatGPT to write ASCII art of a word for you, and it will write something that really looks like ASCII art of a word. But if you ask it for ASCII art of the word &quot;bear,&quot; it might give you ASCII art of the word &quot;lamppost.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T11:41:19-07:00","id":1522279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1522216-ai-chat-as-a-possible-storyteller-s-tool?p=1522244#post1522244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an example of expecting a Large Language Model to &quot;understand&quot; the material it's fed.<br /> <br /> A Large Language Model does one thing: it produces a convincing, plausible, real-<i>sounding</i> answer to a question or prompt. Not an accurate or a well-crafted answer. It's a pattern-matching machine; it finds and matches patterns without understanding the context that produces them. If you feed it Charm text, its output will match the Charm format pattern, having Charm names, costs in motes and Willpower, keywords (but not necessarily always keywords that <i>exist,</i> let alone keywords used correctly for how they work), and descriptions of actions. There is no reason to expect it will be able to associate the relative game balance of different opportunity costs and desired effects.<br /> <br /> You can ask ChatGPT to write ASCII art of a word for you, and it will write something that really looks like ASCII art of a word. But if you ask it for ASCII art of the word &quot;bear,&quot; it might give you ASCII art of the word &quot;lamppost.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>for sure, its not a set it and forget it type thing, it is something that you can use to do some of the leg work for you and you have to proof everything it creates<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T21:58:18-07:00","id":1522556,"title":"","content":"I and my ST have found it useful for somewhat on the fly or stuff when we're just stuck. You know stuff like, &quot;I need a silly sounding drink name&quot; or a quick generator for a bar tender etc. I used it to give me a general idea of an invocation when I wasn't sure how else to do it. (For the record I was essentially serving a legal summons to a local spirit court on an island to report for questioning about the crap the circle was there for.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-18T11:44:42-07:00","id":1522756,"title":"","content":"Yes, its a good one stop shop if you run online sometimes you hunt down a fantasy name generator online but the outputs are very Dungeons and Dragons and you end up wasting time while with a Large Language Model you can literally tell it that the output sucks and what you're looking for instead if it does that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T19:04:28-07:00","id":1532932,"title":"","content":"Definitely can help when I'm stuck on something and come up with ideas I haven't thought of. But for sure, if overused i find that i become way too dependant on ChatGPT and a lot of what it spouts is actually just garbage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T03:04:15-07:00","id":1533374,"title":"","content":"ChatGPT is an excellent <b>support </b>tool for any Storyteller or Player. I use it to brainstorm ideas, organize my adventures and campaigns, or when I need to come up with something on the fly. That said, I will echo what some people have already mentioned: ChatGPT can help you improve your work but can't do the work for you. The main problems with ChatGPT as some have pointed out are that it doesn't understand context because there's no real intelligence behind it, and everything it throws at you will always skew heavily towards the most average response. As it stands now, ChatGPT can't substitute a real storyteller, there's no passion or originality in anything it creates. However, ask me again in 5 or 10 years and I may give you a different answer, it's scary how fast this technology is advancing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T17:48:56-07:00","id":1533398,"title":"","content":"And as with the old ways of flipping a coin, sometimes its good just to have something to look at and go, &quot;Nope not that.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}